#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725695 :multistep/context "Source question: assignment PDF page 4, parts (a)–(d); page 5 is workspace.\n\nNewton’s law of cooling gives $T\\prime(t)+kT(t)=kT_m(t)$, $T(0)=T_0$, where temperature changes in proportion to the difference between the object and its surroundings. A soda starts at $20^\\circ C$ in a cooler at constant $3^\\circ C$. After 10 minutes its temperature is $15^\\circ C$. Determine how long it takes to reach $5^\\circ C$ through the steps below." :multistep/id #uuid "be3a2879-9608-5b87-9339-2abff9c5057c" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725646 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725739}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725651 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725571}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725698 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725614}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725706 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725699}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725720 :multistep/context "Source question: [WeBWorK Problem 4](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_3/4).\n\nA thermometer moves from a room at $22^\\circ C$ to outdoors at $-1^\\circ C$. After one minute it reads $12^\\circ C$." :multistep/id #uuid "e1496846-f368-546e-9d05-0961ebd413e3" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725550 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725556}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725717 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725733}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725742 :multistep/context "Source question: [WeBWorK Problem 3](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_3/3).\n\nCarbon-14 is replenished while an organism lives, then decays at a rate proportional to its amount after death. Use the source’s half-life of 5,597 years, and let $C(t)$ be its amount after $t$ years." :multistep/id #uuid "fc994318-b020-5189-ac90-7884b95d2091" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725558 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725576}} {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218672565